title: 5. A reader's journal.
pid: 2bbef69a-c9f8-4efe-8a4d-7af3a43ac298
body: |2-
  The follower's server keeps the last version it loaded of each foreign
  node; it already reloads foreign files when they change, and Ed's
  daemon announced such a change but had lost the old text. The baseline
  is what this reader last had. It needs no Git on the author's side,
  catches uncommitted work, and keeps the old text, so a report can say
  what changed and not only that something did. It costs storage about
  the size of the foreign data one reads, and "my server loaded it" is
  not "I read it".
